# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BuyVanda — web environment
#
# EVERYTHING IN THIS FILE SHIPS TO THE BROWSER.
# Vite compiles VITE_-prefixed values into the bundle, where anyone can read
# them in devtools. There is no such thing as a secret here.
#
# Server secrets live in the root .env, which Vite never opens — leave
# `envDir` alone in vite.config.ts and it stays that way.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Step 0 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000


# ── Step 1 — Cognito ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These two are public by design: they identify which pool to sign in
# against, they do not grant access to it. The client SECRET is not here
# and must never be — it lives in the root .env, used only by the API.
VITE_AWS_REGION=
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=
